rms  that he'd like to see in place right in  the past 48 hours we've seen the  Republican governor move forward on  legislation around background checks and  rad flag laws we've seen the Republican  congressman here call for the end of  these assault weapons I'm pleased with  all of those those efforts the president  has a choice of lots of options to take  actions to make sure that these  senseless gun crime these guns which are  legal right now these senseless gun  actions slow down one example is the the  red flag law that Lindsey Graham and  Blumenthal have moved forward he could  support that and say I'm going to I'm  going to do everything it's president to  make that happen  we know the president is someone that  relishes action  but we've seen no action around gun  issues just a lot of talk Mara Whaley  the gunman's family released a statement  saying that they are cooperating with  law enforcement have you learned  anything new about the gunman's motives  we haven't yesterday afternoon the FBI  took over that section of the  investigation because of some of the  violent ideologies is what they've what  they've talked about but they've also  said that they're pretty confident that  it's not racially motivated so we'll  leave that to the federal investigators  to really under that you went to two  hospitals to visit some of the shooting  survivors and the medical teams how is  everyone holding up look it's tough you  know when I went to visit the folks that  were injured they had you know lost a  friend their other friends were there so  this is like not just one person that  just was sitting here and nobody was  else surrounded so their whole network  of folks have had great trauma around  what happened Saturday night and that's  going to take some time for our  community a lot of a lot of those  injured are just processing not really  understanding you know really what  happened and you know look though the  whole community is still processing that  we have survivors all over this  community there were over thousands of  people here in the district Saturday  night like a normal Saturday night so  we're all in that process but certainly  the the families who lost loved ones and  those that have been injured are people  that we're paying very close attention  to here in Dayton mayor Whaley  unfortunately so many have been in your  shoes before have you gotten any advice  that may help you as you try to lead  your community in healing now yeah the  the mayor's across the country have been  terrific not surprisingly you know  mayors are the last functioning part of  government so Bill Peduto Pittsburgh has  been in touch with me every single day a  Christine Hough chomsky the mayor of  Parkland has been amazing mayor caster  down in Tampa Florida it used to be a  police chief has been awesome and Buddy  Dyer of Orlando with the pulse nightclub  unfortunately this is a fraternity that  we wish didn't exist but I am so  grateful for the mayors across the  country their leadership and their want  an action to finally make it so we don't  have to have another city that continues  to go through with this you have that  list just far too long  mayor Whaley thank you  again our condolences to all of you  there in Dayton thank you
 

